    "proposed_facts": [
      {
        "index": 0,
        "supported": true,
        "reason": "Canonical sentinel handling clears only stat fields and resets the cursor; subsequent format switches read ent. Recognized formats can therefore produce offsets starting at zero and nonzero offsetData. Default branches and banner/shared-icon palette handling support the remaining claims."
      },
      {
        "index": 1,
        "supported": true,
        "reason": "Canonical setter guards, access rejection, mutation ordering, and immediate failure cleanup match the proposal. CARDDir.c confirms successful-write directory switching and mirroring, conditional release when apiCallback is null, and eraseCallback clearing before notification on completion or errors. Successful erase-to-write scheduling returns before cleanup. No local mutation rollback occurs."
      }
    ],
